    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d572">

                <pb facs="0725" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg601"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2199: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Technical Board</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-11T10:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                                1921—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:38
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>In connection with my cipher telegram August 10, 10 a.m., through Tokyo<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d572-f1"/> in regard to the loan, following conditions must
                    obtain:</p>
                <p>1st. Technical Board must have control over all receipts and expenditures. 2d.
                    Proceeds of loan to be placed in the hands of Board which shall have sole charge
                    of expenditure for the benefit of railway in its judgment. 3d. Other than
                    members of Board, no person shall be retained in the service of railway in
                    opposition to determinations of that nature [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Board</hi>]. The last condition is to prevent the Chinese from loading payroll
                    with high positions for their men as they are now doing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d572-f1" n="33" xml:id="d572-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 272, Aug. 11, from the Chargé in Japan, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
